# The Weston pin: Debian's own weston source package, fetched from the archive at the snapshot pin
# (debian-packaging/snapshot.list's first source) and rebuilt with this directory's patches
# added to its quilt series (patches/series) as WESTON_LOCAL_VERSION, which sorts above Debian's.
# The weston stage of debian-packaging/builder/Dockerfile fetches it, refuses a .dsc whose sha256
# is not WESTON_DSC_SHA256 and installs its Build-Depends; dpkg-source checks the tarballs against
# the .dsc; debian-packaging/build-weston.sh builds it. Its weston and libweston-14-0 join the
# local repo, and photo-wall-node-display Depends on both at exactly WESTON_LOCAL_VERSION
# (debian/rules reads this file as ${weston:Version}). The only place either version is written:
# a Debian update or a patch change moves WESTON_LOCAL_VERSION (+photowallN) with it
# (docs/module-debian-packaging.md, "Bump or re-patch Weston").
# Plain NAME=value lines: sh, make and Python read them alike.
WESTON_VERSION=14.0.2-1
WESTON_LOCAL_VERSION=14.0.2-1+photowall1
WESTON_DSC_SHA256=7c06118894b6274212f68e61c138a87ccbb869a5d3835aaa543570c004f8ec65
